    {
      "id": "mandarin_disjoint_emphasis",
      "article_id": "34125090-b480-4d63-b13a-33d47470f335",
      "title": "A Call to Holiness",
      "language": "cmn",
      "source_html": "<article data-article-id=\"34125090-b480-4d63-b13a-33d47470f335\">\n<p><em>And when he saw their faith, he said unto him, Man, thy sins are forgiven thee –Luke 5:20.</em> They sought healing, but Jesus saw the deeper need of this man’s soul, so He offered forgiveness. This, of course, raised the ire of the Pharisees who <em>…began to reason, saying, Who is this which speaketh blasphemies? Who can forgive sins, but God alone? –Luke 5:21.</em> They were right, only God can forgive sins, but what they did not want to believe was that Jesus was God’s Son and that thus He had did have the power to forgive sins. So, Jesus went on to say: <em>…What reason ye in your hearts? Whether is easier, to say, Thy sins be forgiven thee; or to say, Rise up and walk? <strong>But that ye may know that the Son of man hath power upon earth to forgive sins</strong>, (he said unto the sick of the palsy,) I say unto thee, Arise, and take up thy couch, and go into thine house –Luke 5:22-24.</em></p>\n<p>In Augustus Toplady’s famous hymn, <em>Rock of Ages</em> we find this line–</p>\n</article>",
      "translation_html": "<article data-article-id=\"34125090-b480-4d63-b13a-33d47470f335\">\n<p><em>耶稣看见他们的信，就对那病人说：人哪，你的罪赦了──路加福音 5:20。</em>他们是来求医治的，但耶稣看见此人灵魂更深的需要，所以他赐下了赦罪。当然，这激怒了法利赛人，他们<em>…心里议论说，这人说僭妄的话了，谁能赦罪，只有神一位能赦──路加福音 5:21。</em>他们说得没错，只有神能赦罪，但他们不愿意相信耶稣是神的儿子，因此也不肯承认他有赦罪的权柄。于是耶稣接着说：<em>你们心里为什么这样议论呢？说：你的罪赦了，容易呢，还是说：起来行走，容易呢？但要叫你们知道人子在地上有赦罪的权柄，（就对那瘫子说，）我吩咐你起床，拿你的褥子回家去吧──路加福音 5:22-24。</em></p>\n<p>在奥古斯都·托普莱迪著名的圣诗《磐石》中，我们找到这句——</p>\n</article>",
      "expected_source_paths": [
        "/article[1]/p[1]/em[3]/strong[1]",
        "/article[1]/p[2]/em[1]"
      ],
