    {
      "id": "cancer_missing_sup",
      "article_id": "d38bf79f-957f-413c-ad4d-a6b4fa8c8112",
      "title": "Cancer… What Is It?",
      "language": "ind",
      "source_html": "<article data-article-id=\"d38bf79f-957f-413c-ad4d-a6b4fa8c8112\">\n<p>We know that before the flood, men lived to be very old—often into their 900s. Mutations must have been rare. Their DNA was closer to the original genetic specimen of mankind (and thus, to perfection) than ours is in the 21<sup>st</sup> century (AD) Therefore, the chance of genes mutating and abnormal genes popping up was much less than it is now.</p>\n</article>",
      "translation_html": "<article data-article-id=\"d38bf79f-957f-413c-ad4d-a6b4fa8c8112\">\n<p>Kita tahu bahwa sebelum banjir, orang hidup sangat tua—sering mencapai usia 900-an. Mutasi pasti jarang. DNA mereka lebih dekat ke spesimen genetik asli umat manusia (dan dengan demikian, ke kesempurnaan) daripada DNA kita di abad ke-21 M. Oleh karena itu, kemungkinan gen bermutasi dan gen abnormal muncul jauh lebih kecil daripada sekarang.</p>\n</article>",
      "expected_source_paths": [
        "/article[1]/p[1]/sup[1]"
      ],
